       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the usual safe limits for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2,000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The standard adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. At 70 kg with normal liver function, 6,000 mg/day carries a real risk of hepatotoxicity.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nWas this a typo? Some options:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily:** 3,000 mg/day.\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily:** 4,000 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours:** 2,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you do want 2,000 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
      }
