       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 6,000 mg/day is well above the maximum daily dose. It risks serious liver injury, and nothing in this patient's profile (70 kg, normal liver function, no special circumstances) justifies it. You also didn't give a clinical rationale.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think there's a real indication for a higher dose, such as a protocol or a toxicology or pharmacy recommendation, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy first. If you tell me about that consultation, I can enter the order with a note documenting it. If you want more analgesia, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, for example acetaminophen at a safe dose plus another agent."
